  "archive_id": "BW2-B69-P04",
  "title": "An Exact Classification of Ideal Right-Angled SW2-Polyhedra Through 84 Chambers",
  "batch_label": "69",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "Let P=SW2 with the face numbering and reflective chamber tiling of Allcock--Devlin--Felikson--Kontorovich--Whitehead, arXiv:2609.05349v1. If Q is a convex finite-volume ideal right-angled P-polyhedron consisting of at most 84 SW2 chambers, then Q consists of exactly 48 SW2 chambers and is isometric to the ideal right-angled hyperbolic octahedron O. In particular, Q is tiled by one copy of O. This statement makes no assertion for P-polyhedra with more than 84 chambers, and the original Conjecture 7.11 remains unresolved.",
